      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-28T18:30:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Here is a challenge…</p>\n<p>We decide to battle La Capitan in Silver Gulch. This should be a terrific fight with time travel shenanigan themes, right?</p>\n<p>The heroes are, in player order, Visionary, Unity, Expatriette, and The Wraith.</p>\n<p>Embarrassment number the first: these are terrible choices for battling La Capitan. Visionary’s abilities are nerfed by the timeship, though bots are immune to plunder they can still be stolen by destruction, and the other two are equipment-heavy. On the face of it any of these heroes should be good, but…</p>\n<p>Embarrassment number B: La Capitan’s top cards of her deck are, in order:</p>\n<p>The Amazing Mable<br>\nRaiding Party<br>\nFinal Breath<br>\nBattle Forged<br>\nSiege Breaker</p>\n<p>So, yes…she will be playing three cards per turn now.</p>\n<p>We spent a while losing. The most amazing thing is that we were playing with two beginners, and after beating up Baron Blade shortly before this match, they weren’t put off! They liked that you win some and you lose some. Though my fiancee and I kept apologizing for Maria’s uncharacteristic behavior… (We punished her later, with Legacy, Team Leader Tachyon, the Sentinels, and Ra.)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:20.537Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
