    {
      "id": 146940,
      "name": "The Burning Stickman",
      "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-29T17:51:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It's a consistency thing, I think -- the higher difficulty villains seem to have a lot of cards that are moderately bad and a few that are a little worse. The lower difficulty villains mostly have cards that aren't all that rough, but have two or three that are devastating (Technological Singularity, Seditive Darts and Devious Disruption, I'm looking at you and glaring).</p><p>Like take The Chairman -- does a lot of damage, mostly. A <em>lot</em> of damage. But that's more or less it -- very little ongoing/equipment destruction, doesn't constrict what you can or can't do. So if you're equipped to deal with the damage in some way, you can handle him. Legacy can single-handedly render the Chairman's entire deck harmless, for instance.</p><p>Matriarch is similar -- if you can consistently keep her from doing retribution damage, you've pretty much already won.</p><p>Then you have Baron Blade, whose cards are varied -- he does damage, too, but not on the same scale, and has more things constricting you (Ongoings and Targets that redirect or counterattack), and works toward his instant-lose condition. They tend not to build on one another, and you can deal with each as they come up fairly simply. And then he has Devious Disruption, which in my experience might as well read, \"Wipe out all your ongoings and equipment, or you lose via TPK.\"</p><p>Omnitron, similarly, splits it up, but takes away the option -- you'll be rebuilding from scratch and probably down a character if he happens to draw up both Seditive Darts and Singularity in one turn -- and I've had Wraith wiped out completely by singularity.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:24:56.856Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
